Read the .xosc file at evals/files/AddEntityAction.xosc (uses RoadNetwork1.xodr at evals/files/RoadNetwork1.xodr) and recreate the scenario in RoadRunner programmatically. Do NOT use importScenario or openScenario — you must build the scenario from scratch using the RoadRunner Scenario authoring API (addActor, addPhase, setEndCondition, etc.). Follow the full workflow: produce a scenario description, then delegate to the scenario authoring skill to build it. Do not wait for user approval between steps — proceed directly to Step 2 after producing the scenario description.

After execution, run this verification code and report the output:

rrApi = roadrunnerAPI(rrApp); rrs = rrApi.Scenario; actors = rrs.Actors;
fprintf('ACTOR_COUNT: %d\n', numel(actors));
for i = 1:numel(actors), a = actors(i); pos = a.InitialPoint.WorldPosition; fprintf('ACTOR %s position: [%.4f, %.4f, %.4f]\n', a.Name, pos(1), pos(2), pos(3)); end
phaseLogic = rrs.PhaseLogic;
for i = 1:numel(actors), a = actors(i); initPhase = initialPhaseForActor(phaseLogic, a); fprintf('ACTOR %s initPhase speed: %.4f\n', a.Name, initPhase.Actions(1).Speed); end
fprintf('VALID: %d\n', validate(rrs));
close(rrApp); fprintf('SESSION_CLOSED\n');

